                        <forename>Robert </forename>
                        <surname>Fellowes</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1771">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1847"/>
                    <occupation>Philanthroppist, editor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Active in the Queen Caroline affair on the side of the Queen, and edited
                            and published the addresses in support of the Queen. Denounced by
                            William Cobbett for inheriting money from Baron Maseres on his death in
                            1825, but defended in <title>The Examiner </title> on January 29, 1826.
                            Godwin approaches Fellowes in 1825, most probably looking to him as a
                            potential benefactor.</p>
                    </note>
